<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:50Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>AfD's Ulrich Siegmund has plans for Saxony-Anhalt and beyond</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c323999fdf20f27828cdf3900895df3a7d1ad1ac5a847e1ca70debeed54706c</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T04:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-s-ulrich-siegmund-has-plans-for-saxony-anhalt-and-beyond/a-78579499--b7bff8d27942.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-s-ulrich-siegmund-has-plans-for-saxony-anhalt-and-beyond/a-78579499?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD's lead candidate in the upcoming election aims to turn his small federal state into a blueprint for right-wing extremist politics across Germany.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US irks Germany, Europe with Russian G20 invite, press bans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ef5c69ec2e24fb5b0da414bbfe02c0fad7b27babb0284b2a319281861714b35</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919--a133d5f50599.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's finance minister is at the G20 meeting in Asheville but some key US press corps members are not. The mood was already tense amid the lengthy Iran war and Trump's renewed beef with neighbor Canada.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Summer was 2nd hottest of the century — DWD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7259211e6d769b4d079c1275c88b3f30a2d442f4a0ad840663f614aae43035d0</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T08:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-summer-was-2nd-hottest-of-the-century-dwd/live-78568957--ff2313dd3357.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-summer-was-2nd-hottest-of-the-century-dwd/live-78568957?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's DWD weather service says the summer was second only to 2003 in terms of average temperatures. It was also unusually dry. In Cologne, police are seeking a man who fired shots at a cafe storefront.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's SPD is fighting for survival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1218ac0909b6431ab84465b2fb817445d6979180cc87319e22919666b1ffb403</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T11:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-spd-is-fighting-for-survival/a-78586448--d16bfd9fddec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-spd-is-fighting-for-survival/a-78586448?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Social Democratic Party SPD is sinking ever deeper into crisis. Voters are turning away, while unrest is growing within its grassroots ranks. Will the upcoming state elections accelerate the party's downward spiral?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt State Premier Schulze takes on far-right AfD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b59422cb3263c97716c3def623406ef655cd9008e1c9c282410c9be9e6932069</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:50Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-state-premier-schulze-takes-on-far-right-afd/a-78509861--77c6eb4a9c49.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-state-premier-schulze-takes-on-far-right-afd/a-78509861?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD is far ahead in the polls in Saxony-Anhalt. But Schulze is determined to keep the AfD from becoming the first far-right party since World War II to lead a German state government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Germany's Merz misstates record in ARD interview</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c111245a425b2bb6c745f045d84bdf184cd25c7520c2b130e4d011c173bda533</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T19:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-merz-misstates-record-in-ard-interview/a-78566319--ff0f9bb5b6d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-merz-misstates-record-in-ard-interview/a-78566319?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz made several misleading claims on migration, debt and electric vehicles in his summer interview with German public broadcaster ARD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>German churches speak out against AfD ahead of state election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08a7f43547d55acf6a5cc9c4b12c71afeebc6e40f60fb59fecbbd3e8d6e89d74</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T15:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-churches-speak-out-against-afd-ahead-of-state-election/a-78482465--9872affc1818.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-churches-speak-out-against-afd-ahead-of-state-election/a-78482465?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the far-right AfD party leads the polls ahead of Sunday's election in Saxony-Anhalt, church leaders have warned against downplaying its "ethnonationalist" agenda.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4765e6e6fad7586d29435c2658a2374d09b1ecddc0a542b7f9c814c2fb9465ab</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--d7968a32f7c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Amanal Petros: From refugee to European champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ea5c43f16912fc8d07b404b180c35c27c0bd22aca18731970cfbc678a785db0</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504--c7c332adab8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amanal Petros fled the Eritrean–Ethiopian war and came to Germany as a teenager. Now one of the world's top marathon runners, he recently won gold at the European Athletics Championships.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Jamal Musiala collapses on pitch again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b19dc0e7e6bc7b223f5f12948161ae53cf04adc59aca288e39e58c2614a5e7c2</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T10:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-jamal-musiala-collapses-on-pitch-again/a-78426021--4f3678c0bd32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-jamal-musiala-collapses-on-pitch-again/a-78426021?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One of Germany's top footballers has collapsed on the pitch for a second time in four days ahead of the new season. Bayern Munich's Jamal Musiala has said he has a "neurological dysfunction" that causes blackouts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>How Germany's Hyrox became a global fitness craze</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ae7021a3accac74e4b25864c60af00b00f8fca912eed243e7aebbdaffac3e63</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T09:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-germany-s-hyrox-became-a-global-fitness-craze/a-78074218--a6c218d1a3af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-germany-s-hyrox-became-a-global-fitness-craze/a-78074218?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Created in Germany and now a global success, Hyrox combines running and functional training into a unique format. How a German concept became an international sports phenomenon.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
